    tag is checked by the build because it is part of the machine template).
  - The machine build commands in foreclose-app/build.sh and fixtures/build.sh
    reproduce the Makefile targets applications/erc20-withdrawal-dapp,
    applications/echo-dapp, applications/mcycle-overflow-dapp,
    applications/unexpected-yield-dapp and applications/invalid-*-dapp.
  - The fixture generator (test/tooling/terminalmachine) and the builder
    image (Dockerfile stage go-prepare) are NOT copied: the build clones the
    tag, checks the commit, and uses them from there.

The machine snapshots also embed third-party binaries that are downloaded at
build time and checked against test/dependencies.sha256 of the same tag:
  - linux-6.5.13-ctsi-2-v0.21.0.bin (cartesi/machine-linux-image v0.21.0)
  - rootfs-tools.ext2 (cartesi/machine-guest-tools v0.18.0)
